quran[17]{c,v,t}:
  23,43,"No nation can advance its term, nor can it delay."
  23,44,"Then We sent Our messengers successively. Whenever a messenger would come to its community, they would deny him. So, We caused them to follow one another and turned them into folktales. So away with the disbelieving people!"
  23,45,"Then We sent Musa (Moses) and his brother Harun (Aaron) with Our signs and a manifest authority,"
  23,46,"to Pharaoh and his chiefs—but they acted arrogantly, and they were oppressive people."
  23,47,So they said: ‘Shall we believe in two humans like ourselves while their people are our slaves?’
  23,48,"They rejected both of them, so they (also) became among those destroyed."
  23,49,We gave Musa (Moses) the Book; perhaps they might follow the right direction.
  23,50,"And We made the son of Maryam (Mary) and his mother a (great) sign. And We gave them shelter on a highland, a place of comfort, watered by a flowing spring."
  23,51,"O messengers! Eat good things and act righteously. Indeed, I am All-Knowing of what you do."
  23,52,"Indeed, this—your community—is one community, and I am your Lord. Therefore, be conscious of Me."
  23,53,But they divided their matter (i.e. their religion) into sects based upon different scriptures. Each group is pleased with what (portion) it has.
  23,54,So leave them in their overwhelming ignorance for a while.
  23,55,"Do they think, since We have provided them with wealth and children,"
  23,56,that We are eager to honour them with all kinds of good? No! They are not aware (of the reality).
  23,57,"Indeed, those who are apprehensive in fear of their Lord,"
  23,58,"and those who believe in the Signs of their Lord,"
  23,59,"and those who do not ascribe partners to their Lord,"
